# DDD Software Delivery

## Description: <br>
Deliver a confirmed client-server software requirement through requirement validation, domain-driven design, separate backend and frontend implementation, integration review, independent testing, operable packaging, and final acceptance. <br>

## Publisher: <br>
DevWerk <br>

## Category: <br>
software_delivery <br>

## Tags: <br>
- software-development <br>
- domain-driven-design <br>
- pair-programming <br>
- frontend-backend-collaboration <br>
- automated-testing <br>
- devops <br>
- release-readiness <br>

## Use Case: <br>
Use for a client-server software delivery scope whose user-visible requirement and acceptance criteria have been confirmed. Backend, frontend, and integration review are separate observable Workflow Columns; implementation Columns can retain their own logical sessions across directed rework. The delivery may target a local package, container, source repository, or an external CI/CD platform. <br>

## Selection Guide: <br>
Select when the work must produce runnable software and verifiable engineering evidence. Continue user conversation instead when product behavior, acceptance criteria, or delivery target remains materially ambiguous. <br>

## Loop Input: <br>
Project name and delivery target are Project bindings. Each Task identifies one confirmed requirement file and its delivery scope. <br>

## Loop Output: <br>
Traceable requirements, domain and interface design, reviewed source code, automated test evidence, operable delivery assets, and final acceptance. <br>

